Races Stay Busy Because of Item Boxes
Item boxes are placed across the courses, and driving through one gives the racer a random item. Some items are used to hit or slow down other racers, while others push the kart forward with extra speed. That means a player in the middle of the pack is not completely stuck there.

Different Karts Change the Feel of a Character
The game starts with eight playable racers and includes Daisy, Dry Bones, Waluigi, and R.O.B. as unlockable characters. Every racer has three karts, and those karts do not handle the same way. Top speed, acceleration, and handling all change how a race feels, especially on tighter corners.

Grand Prix Mixes New and Returning Tracks
Mario Kart DS includes 32 courses across eight cups. Some tracks are new for this Nintendo DS release, while others return from older Mario Kart games. Baby Park is one of the returning tracks, and its short layout makes item hits feel harder to avoid.


## Engine Classes Make Races Faster

Grand Prix and Versus races use 50cc, 100cc, and 150cc classes. Higher classes make every kart faster, so turns arrive sooner and recovery after an item hit becomes more important. Mirror mode also flips the tracks horizontally while using 150cc speed.


## Mission Mode Breaks Away from Normal Cups

